---
import ReadingLayout from "../layouts/ReadingLayout.astro";
import { asset } from "../data/project";
---

<ReadingLayout
  title="Accessibility and assistance"
  description="Reading options and accessibility assistance for the HOIST research project."
>
  <h1>Accessibility and assistance</h1>
  <p>
    We aim to make this research website usable by everyone, following WCAG 2.1
    Level AA.
  </p>
  <h2>Reading and viewing options</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Read the <a href={asset("paper/")}>full paper in HTML</a> or the <a
        href={asset("supplementary/")}>supplementary material in HTML</a
      >. These versions include headings, table headers, mathematical notation,
      and figure descriptions.
    </li><li>
      Silent clips accompany the <a href={asset("") + "#overview"}>abstract</a>,
      <a href={asset("") + "#method"}>method</a>, and
      <a href={asset("") + "#results"}>results</a>. They start automatically when
      visible, unless reduced motion or data saving is enabled. Use each player’s
      native controls to pause or resume; a manual pause is respected when scrolling.
      Every clip has timed visual descriptions and an expandable text description.
      Source credits for the introductory clips appear below the introduction.
    </li><li>
      Results are available as labeled numbers and tables. Color is not the only
      way to distinguish methods or outcomes.
    </li><li>
      All controls support a keyboard. Use Tab to move between controls, Enter
      to follow links, Space or Enter to activate buttons, and the arrow keys to
      switch result tabs.
    </li><li>The page supports browser zoom and reduced-motion preferences.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Request assistance or report a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    If you have trouble using this site or need research materials in another
    format, email <a href="mailto:liusongyang@ufl.edu"
      >Songyang Liu at liusongyang@ufl.edu</a
    >. Please include the page or material involved and describe what is not
    working. Do not send sensitive medical information.
  </p>
  <h2>Evaluation</h2>
  <p>
    We use automated axe checks together with keyboard, responsive-layout,
    text-spacing, and content reviews. Automated checks alone do not establish
    complete WCAG conformance. Research documents and media are reviewed
    separately from the webpage.
  </p>
</ReadingLayout>
